      },
      "message": "test(ui): frame-cost probe names the cost of each still-frame piece\n\nAdd `frame_cost` spans (a no-op flag read unless a probe records) over\nthe commands, scene and UI pieces of a frame, and the headless probe\n`frame_cost_probe::still_frames_on_fig8_name_their_costs`. It measures\nsix still frames of fig8.step in five states and asserts counts only\n(no chain walk, no digest; one collection per scene; the Boundary\npreview runs only while its group is open).\n\nRecord the frame-cost rule in docs/decisions/2238-frame-cost-rule.md\n(cache key order, the writer invalidates, the layer, two tests per\ncache, the safety line, the simulation keyframes) and its short form\nin crates/ui/AGENTS.md.\n\ntestdata/models/fig8.step is taken unchanged from main (#2215) for the\nprobe.\n\nNo behaviour change.\n\nRefs #2238\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
